                <pb facs="0308" n="190" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg190"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">838.5045/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the High Commissioner in
                        Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-12-04T20:00:00-05:00">December 4, 1929—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>60. Your 90 December 4 noon. The Department does not desire you to take such
                    measures as you describe unless absolutely necessary for the protection of
                    lives. The situation as you have described it does not seem to make such
                    measures necessary.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
